Subject: [MFVEA] Validate D3D11 texture format and copy bounds in mf_helpers

Validate that VideoFrame::format() is compatible with the underlying
D3D11 texture DXGI_FORMAT and check visible_rect bounds and 2x2
alignment against the actual D3D11_TEXTURE2D_DESC before copying.

Bug: 574791611
Change-Id: I94d27fe2c5e1ad34be9e1db63c4eb14cc57e095a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8614061
Reviewed-by: Eugene Zemtsov <eugene@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Eugene Zemtsov <eugene@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1724397}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
media/base/win/mf_helpers.cc on this branch carried inline 4:2:0 visible_rect alignment checks at the two copy sites; as upstream, they are replaced by the new ValidateCopySubresourceBox() check.

